course: dictionary
lesson: 10947
title: Waist: the middle of your body
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your waist is the middle part of your body, between your ribs and your hips. It is usually the narrowest part of you, and it is where a belt goes. «An ant's narrow waist has one or two small bumps called nodes» uses the same idea: the waist is the thin part in the middle.
explain: Waist has a second meaning too. The waist of a piece of clothing is the part that goes around your waist, such as the waistband of a skirt. Look at the words around the word to see which meaning is being used.
explain: Water can be measured by your waist too. «Waist-deep» water reaches up to your middle. Swimming teachers use it as a safety guide, because moving water can knock you over even when it only comes up to your waist.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The Duchess says she won't put her arm round Alice's waist.» Put in "the middle of the body" and it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Your waist is the middle part of your body, between your ribs and your hips.
fact: The waist is usually the narrowest part of your body, and it is where a belt goes.
fact: «Waist-deep» water reaches up to your middle.
fact: Moving water can knock you over even when it is only waist-deep, so always stay safe.
fact: «Love handles» is a joking name for fat around the waist.
exercise: «A girl in Christchurch learns rugby: her coach shows her how to tackle low around the waist and legs.» Where does she tackle? | The hands and arms | *The waist and legs, low down | The shoulders only | The head and neck
exercise: What is the waistband of a skirt? | The hem at the bottom | A pocket on the side | *The part of the clothing that goes around your waist | A belt loop on the back
exercise: «Love handles» is a joking name for what? | Muscles in the arms | A kind of handbag | A type of sports equipment | *Fat around the waist
test: If the water is waist-deep, how far up your body does it reach? | Up to your ankles | Up to the top of your head | Up to your neck | *Up to your middle
test: Which two parts of the body does your waist lie between? | Your shoulders and your head | *Your ribs and your hips | Your knees and your feet | Your elbows and your wrists
exam: Why must you be careful in waist-deep water? | Because the water is always cold | Because waist-deep water is always dirty | *Because moving water can knock you over even at that depth | Because fish will bite your legs
